Each equality check from the if/else-if ladder becomes a case label, else becomes
default; break exits the switch (execution continues after the closing brace — break
does not terminate the program). Both programs give the same messages for all
grades A/B/C/D/F and W. Multiple case labels are placed one after another:
switch (ch) {
case 'Y':
/* ch == 'Y' */
/* do something */
break;
case 'N':
/* ch == 'N' */
/* do something else */
break;
default:
/* otherwise */
/* do a third thing */
break;
}
switch (ch) {
case 'Y':
case 'y':
/* do something if ch == 'Y' or ch == 'y' */
break;
}
