The base case must be reachable: having a base case in the code doesn’t guarantee
termination. A recursive call with the same n prints 3, 3, 3, 3 . . . — the input never
reaches 0; the fix is countdown(n - 1). Negative input for this simple function would
still break it — the input contract (n >= 0) is important; unbounded recursion can
exhaust the stack:
void count_down(int n)
