P11. Missing & in scanf
int x;
scanf("%d", x);
printf("%d\n", x);
P11. What does scanf(”%d”, x) do without &?
Answer. scanf needs the address of a variable; passing x (uninitialized int) makes
scanf treat its garbage value as a pointer and write to that address — undefined
behavior; most compilers warn with -Wall. Fix: scanf(”%d”, &x);.
int x;
scanf("%d", &x;);
printf("%d\n", x);
