P12. Use after free
int *p = malloc(sizeof(int));
*p = 42;
free(p);
printf("%d\n", *p);
P12. Why printing *p after free(p) is an error?
Answer. After free(p), the memory may already be reused: reading p may print 42,
garbage, or crash (use after free — undefined behavior). By key: don’t touch p after
free; print before freeing; after free assign p = NULL to make the error loud:
int *p = malloc(sizeof(int));
*p = 42;
printf("%d\n", *p);
free(p);
p = NULL;
